course: dictionary
lesson: 14632
title: Poultry on the farm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Poultry is a group word. It means farm birds, such as chickens, ducks, geese and turkeys, that are kept for their meat or their eggs. «The farmer keeps poultry in a big barn.» Here poultry means all the birds together, not just one hen.
explain: Poultry is uncountable, so we do not say "a poultry" or "two poultries". We say "some poultry" or "the poultry". The word can also mean the meat from these birds: «We ate roast poultry for Sunday lunch.»
explain: Use the clues around the word. Look for words like farm, eggs, hens or meat. Then swap in a bird you know, such as chicken or duck, and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, your meaning is right.
fact: Poultry means farm birds that are kept for their meat or eggs.
fact: Chickens, ducks, geese and turkeys are all kinds of poultry.
fact: «Poultry» can also mean the meat from these birds, as in «raw poultry», which is meat that has not been cooked.
fact: Always wash your hands after touching raw poultry, and cook it thoroughly so it is safe to eat.
fact: «Free-range poultry» are birds that can move about outdoors, instead of being kept in a small space.
exercise: «The poultry farm has hens, ducks and geese.» What is a poultry farm? | *A farm where birds are kept for meat or eggs | A shop that sells bread | A park with ponds for wild ducks | A farm that grows only wheat and corn
exercise: «Always wash your hands after touching raw poultry.» What does raw poultry mean? | *Uncooked meat from farm birds | Eggs boiled in a pan | Fish from a river | Cooked meat in a sandwich
exercise: Which of these is a kind of poultry? | Cow | Pig | *Turkey | Salmon
test: «Free-range poultry can walk around outside.» What does free-range poultry mean? | Birds kept in a small cage all day | *Farm birds that can move about outdoors | Fish kept in a pond | Wild birds that fly over the sea
test: «We had poultry and fish at the party.» In this sentence, what does poultry most likely mean? | *The meat from farm birds | A kind of soup | A large wooden box | A type of vegetable
exam: «The poultry farm sells eggs and chicken.» Which word in the sentence tells you the farm keeps birds for food? | sells | *poultry | farm | eggs
